147:"**Distance sites.** With your first two patches and L's (not the sibling's), the probe measured 54 to 49: :2493 yours and L's four, the crash row gone, no site new (section 6). On your tree: :2493 and the crash row :2886-2999 go, and none come; the sibling's effect on the distance is not measured, so read the table by row and line. Run the count and distance stages once on your final tree, before from climb batch 14's landed tables. Your count is 1, its error body(i) at :1314; its time shows the normal form's effect on the api check, which row 688's memo brought within the limit, against batch 14's gate (under 5 minutes) and the 900 s limit; a first run past 690 s is a point to report, with the api check's time. Then run the count stage once more on your final tree with one line changed for that run only and restored after it, so that git diff shows nothing of it: body(i) at Library/FortressLibrary.fss:1314 written body(i: I): L. Never commit that line: rung B lands it, and with your row 680 repair the gate's stage then checks the library component whole for the first time. This run is the batch's one measure of that stage: report its time and its table (by reading about 43 errors, the component's 36 typecheck and 8 wellformed sites less your :2493, F-53's rise). If it prints no total or takes more than 690 s, do not land row 680's line: land the normal form and the sibling, and report. 690 s leaves room within the 900 s limit for the 27 % the stages slowed under load (the probe's 2,185 s against the 1,714 s of batch 14's gate).",
